From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings > Help, the guide on the device

ChromeOS's help is Google's Help app and support site, which NickelOS
doesn't have, so Settings had no help at all (0056 took About's "Get help"
out). Settings now has Help at the bottom of its menu (Dresden,
2026-11-04): a page of the About section, chrome://os-settings/help/guide,
with its own menu entry, which the menu marks when it's open. Its rows open
the NickelOS guide as it came with this version of the OS (the guide's
pages, the Learning Gentoo page and Troubleshooting, from
chromeos-base/nickel-guide in /usr/share/chromeos-assets/nickel-guide,
where Chrome may open local files) in a browser tab, so they work offline;
and the community page and the guide on nickelos.dev. NickelHelpHandler
opens the local pages (a page name, checked; the website's page if the OS
has no copy of it).

---
